<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Markio opens files the reader chooses, one window per document, and
      does nothing else with the system. The sandbox therefore needs read
      access to user-selected files — and bookmarks to keep them.

      A document comes with access to itself and not to the folder it sits in,
      so the picture beside it cannot be read: there is no entitlement that
      widens a document to its folder, only the reader pointing at that folder
      in a panel. The app-scope bookmark entitlement is what lets that grant
      survive a relaunch, so the reader is asked once and not every morning.

      There is deliberately no network entitlement. A sandboxed WKWebView needs
      com.apple.security.network.client to bring up its content process even
      when it never loads anything — Markio has no web view at all, so the
      grant has nothing to enable and stays out.

      This repository only declares these entitlements. Signing with them
      happens outside it.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-only</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.bookmarks.app-scope</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
